-- title:
--   Invariants of a flat base change of an admissible G-algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, $\pi \in \mathcal O$ irreducible, and suppose $\mathcal O$ is complete for the $\pi$-adic topology (`IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {π})`). Let $R$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra that is $\pi$-adically complete, on which the image of $\pi$ is a nonzerodivisor, and with $R/\pi R$ of finite type over $\mathcal O$; let $G$ be a finite group acting on $R$ by ring automorphisms commuting with the $\mathcal O$-action, and write $A := R^G$ for the invariant $\mathcal O$-subalgebra `FixedPoints.subalgebra 𝒪 R G`. Let $S$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra, $A'$ a flat $A$-algebra, and $\sigma : S \to A'$ a ring homomorphism compatible with the structure maps from $\mathcal O$. Let $R'$ be an $S$-algebra with a $G$-action by ring automorphisms commuting with the $S$-action, $\pi$-adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ from $S$, and with that image a nonzerodivisor on $R'$. Assume given, for every $n$, a ring isomorphism $\tau_n$ from $(R \otimes_A A')/(\pi^{n+1}\otimes 1)$ onto $R'/\pi^{n+1}$, such that: if $\tau_{n+1}$ sends the class of $z$ to the class of $y$ then so does $\tau_n$; if $\tau_n$ sends the class of $x \otimes w$ to the class of $y$ then it sends the class of $(g\cdot x)\otimes w$ to the class of $g\cdot y$, for all $g \in G$; and $\tau_n$ sends the class of $1 \otimes \sigma(s)$ to the class of the image of $s$ in $R'$. The conclusion is twofold: the invariant subalgebra $A'' := (R')^G$ (`FixedPoints.subalgebra S R' G`) is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$; and there exist ring isomorphisms $\alpha_n : A'/\sigma(\pi)^{n+1} \to A''/\pi^{n+1}$ for all $n$ such that (i) if $\alpha_{n+1}$ sends the class of $w$ to the class of $x$ then so does $\alpha_n$, (ii) whenever $\alpha_n$ sends the class of $w$ to the class of $x$, $\tau_n$ sends the class of $1 \otimes w$ to the class of $x$ viewed in $R'$, and (iii) $\alpha_n$ sends the class of $\sigma(s)$ to the class of the image of $s$ in $A''$, for every $s \in S$.
--
--   This is the purely algebraic half of the statement that forming $G$-invariants commutes with a flat base change in the setting of $\pi$-adically complete, $\pi$-torsion-free algebras of finite type modulo $\pi$: the levelwise isomorphisms $\tau_n$ identifying $R \otimes_A A'$ with $R'$ modulo powers of $\pi$ are transported to identifications of $A'$ with $(R')^G$ modulo powers of $\pi$. It is used in the construction of the primed chart package of a base-changed tower quotient datum, where $A'$ arises as a localisation of $A \otimes_{\mathcal O} S$ and $R'$ as the limit chart ring over the corresponding basic opens.
